+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling One Stays Out
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Narrows NG-5 as confirmed by [ADR-2026-08-08](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined both changing and cancelling a visit once booked, and the 2026-08-08 ADR confirmed the row as deliberate. That ADR also set the path for narrowing it: an owner decision recorded at intake, with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+A request on 2026-09-29 asked for booked visits to be correctable. The owner decided on NG-5 at the same intake, quoted verbatim:
+
+> Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner decision above.
+2. **Withdraw NG-5 entirely.** Rejected: the owner kept cancellation out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, under the Visits requirements in the PRD. Cancelling a booked visit remains a deliberate non-goal. NG-4 is unaffected: no visit is ever deleted.
+
+The owner also decided that the correction is reachable by going to it directly, and that no page links to it in this request. A visible entry point may come as a follow-up request. It is deferred, not declined, so it is recorded as an open question rather than as a non-goal.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The 2026-08-08 statement that a booked visit is immutable no longer holds for its date and description.
+- A visit still has no lifecycle state: it is never cancelled, only corrected.
+- The PRD records the narrowed NG-5 row and the new Visits requirement together.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#visits) — the correction requirement the narrowing admits.
